{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4a9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07518-079c-74f3-9ecd-fd15c4068145"},"sequence":175,"recorded_at":1780531400000345,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"8d005352-b4b0-45ba-8943-e8c53777a571"},"task_id":"8d005352-b4b0-45ba-8943-e8c53777a571","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"8d005352-b4b0-45ba-8943-e8c53777a571","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessadapter/identity_census_test.go`.\n1|package sessadapter\n2|\n3|// This file is the identity-gate census (review rev4 B7). It exists\n4|// because the zero-value / absent-fact class was closed three\n5|// times as a site list (4, then 5, then 13 sites) while the class\n6|// stayed open: TestEnvelopeEchoEmptyStringRefuses derives its rows\n7|// from three envelopes with a tripwire that forbids growth, so it\n8|// cannot reach DecodeProbe's schema echo — the identical two lines\n9|// as DecodeManifest's pinned echo — nor CheckProbe, Discover,\n10|// CheckTupleAdmission, or VerifyRequestDigest.\n11|//\n12|// Shape, modelled on TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered:\n13|// scanIdentityGateIDs derives every X != Y and X == Y domain\n14|// comparison from production source (excluding error, nil, EOF,\n15|// delimiter, and length plumbing), and TestIdentityGatesAreCensused\n16|// requires the derived multiset to equal identityRegistrations\n17|// exactly. Both spellings are derived: the zero-fact class is\n18|// spelled both ways in production (Discover refuses `== \"\"`\n19|// while the binding echoes refuse `!=`), and an ==-spelled gate\n20|// with no row used to pass the whole suite unrostered (review\n21|// rev5/F1). A new identity gate with no row fails the census; a\n22|// removed gate orphans its row. Map-presence defaults (!present)\n23|// live in presenceRegistrations with a structural fail-closed\n24|// proof plus behavioral drivers. Vocabulary-table membership\n25|// positives (`x == allowed` over a rostered table) are derived\n26|// here and driven by TestVocabularyMembershipRefusesEmpty, which\n27|// refuses the empty string at every loop; the tables themselves\n28|// stay pinned by TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered. An\n29|// empty scan fails closed, and canaries from the review traversal\n30|// guard scanner blindness in both spellings.\n31|//\n32|// Every non-exempt row names its driver: the committed test\n33|// refusing the zero/absent fact at the exported entry, on the\n34|// side the mutant would exempt. Struct-taking gates (CheckProbe,\n35|// CheckTupleAdmission, CheckBindingEquality) are driven with\n36|// struct literals; bytes-reachable gates (DecodeProbe schema)\n37|// through raw bodies. Where honest decode makes a zero\n38|// unreachable, the row is an explicit exemption naming the\n39|// upstream guard — checkValidateResult's mode echo (vocabulary\n40|// gate at operations.go:1084) is the real example — never a\n41|// silent omission.\n42|//\n43|// Stated bounds: vacuous agreement of two hand-built empty\n44|// structs (an all-zero Probe against all-zero facts) is outside\n45|// the threat model — honest decode never yields empty provider\n46|// identifiers (providerIDPattern) or digests (checkDigest) — and\n47|// stays admitted, documented per row rather than redefined here.\n48|\n49|import (\n50|\t\"go/ast\"\n51|\t\"go/parser\"\n52|\t\"go/token\"\n53|\t\"os\"\n54|\t\"path/filepath\"\n55|\t\"sort\"\n56|\t\"strconv\"\n57|\t\"strings\"\n58|\t\"testing\"\n59|)\n60|\n61|// identityRegistration is one production identity gate with its\n62|// proof: the behavioral zero-row driver, or an explicit\n63|// exemption. domain groups rows for sibling tripwires.\n64|type identityRegistration struct {\n65|\tid     string\n66|\tdriver string\n67|\tdomain string\n68|\texempt bool\n69|\treason string\n70|}\n71|\n72|// scanIdentityGateIDs derives every X != Y and X == Y\n73|// comparison from production source, excluding the mechanical\n74|// classes: error and fault checks, nil presence, io.EOF framing,\n75|// rune delimiters and escapes, and length comparisons (rostered\n76|// by the bound census instead). The spelling split is\n77|// deliberate: identityGatesInSyntax derives both operators with\n78|// identical exclusions, and the synthetic\n79|// TestIdentityScanSeesBothSpellings proves it.\n80|func scanIdentityGateIDs(t *testing.T, directory string) []string {\n81|\tt.Helper()\n82|\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(directory)\n83|\tif err != nil {\n84|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"identity census: %v\", err)\n85|\t}\n86|\tvar ids []string\n87|\tscanned := 0\n88|\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n89|\t\tname := entry.Name()\n90|\t\tif entry.IsDir() || !strings.HasSuffix(name, \".go\") || strings.HasSuffix(name, \"_test.go\") {\n91|\t\t\tcontinue\n92|\t\t}\n93|\t\tscanned++\n94|\t\tpath := filepath.Join(directory, name)\n95|\t\tsource, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n96|\t\tif err != nil {\n97|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"identity census: %v\", err)\n98|\t\t}\n99|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(token.NewFileSet(), path, source, 0)\n100|\t\tif err != nil {\n101|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"identity census: %v\", err)\n102|\t\t}\n103|\t\tids = append(ids, identityGatesInSyntax(syntax, name)...)\n104|\t}\n105|\tif scanned == 0 {\n106|\t\tt.Fatal(\"identity census scanned zero production files; the scanner is broken, not the package\")\n107|\t}\n108|\treturn ids\n109|}\n110|\n111|// identityGatesInSyntax derives the gate identities of one parsed\n112|// production file: every != and == domain comparison with the\n113|// mechanical classes excluded. Both operators share the exclusion\n114|// set, so neither spelling can hide from the roster. Ordinals\n115|// disambiguate repeated spellings inside one function.\n116|func identityGatesInSyntax(syntax *ast.File, name string) []string {\n117|\tvar ids []string\n118|\tfor _, declaration := range syntax.Decls {\n119|\t\tfunction, ok := declaration.(*ast.FuncDecl)\n120|\t\tif !ok || function.Body == nil {\n121|\t\t\tcontinue\n122|\t\t}\n123|\t\tordinal := map[string]int{}\n124|\t\tast.Inspect(function.Body, func(node ast.Node) bool {\n125|\t\t\tcomparison, ok := node.(*ast.BinaryExpr)\n126|\t\t\tif !ok || (comparison.Op != token.NEQ && comparison.Op != token.EQL) {\n127|\t\t\t\treturn true\n128|\t\t\t}\n129|\t\t\tif isNilIdent(comparison.X) || isNilIdent(comparison.Y) {\n130|\t\t\t\treturn true\n131|\t\t\t}\n132|\t\t\tif isErrIdent(comparison.X) || isErrIdent(comparison.Y) {\n133|\t\t\t\treturn true\n134|\t\t\t}\n135|\t\t\tif isEOFSelector(comparison.X) || isEOFSelector(comparison.Y) {\n136|\t\t\t\treturn true\n137|\t\t\t}\n138|\t\t\tif hasRuneLiteral(comparison) {\n139|\t\t\t\treturn true\n140|\t\t\t}\n141|\t\t\tif hasLenCall(comparison) {\n142|\t\t\t\treturn true\n143|\t\t\t}\n144|\t\t\tbase := name + \"|\" + function.Name.Name + \"|\" + renderBoundExpr(comparison)\n145|\t\t\tids = append(ids, base+\"|\"+strconv.Itoa(ordinal[base]))\n146|\t\t\tordinal[base]++\n147|\t\t\treturn true\n148|\t\t})\n149|\t}\n150|\treturn ids\n151|}\n152|\n153|// isNilIdent reports whether the expression is the nil identifier.\n154|func isNilIdent(node ast.Expr) bool {\n155|\tident, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n156|\treturn ok && ident.Name == \"nil\"\n157|}\n158|\n159|// isErrIdent reports whether the expression is an error plumbing\n160|// identifier rather than a domain fact.\n161|func isErrIdent(node ast.Expr) bool {\n162|\tident, ok := node.(*ast.Ident)\n163|\treturn ok && (ident.Name == \"err\" || ident.Name == \"fault\" || ident.Name == \"faultErr\")\n164|}\n165|\n166|// isEOFSelector reports whether the expression is io.EOF.\n167|func isEOFSelector(node ast.Expr) bool {\n168|\tselector, ok := node.(*ast.SelectorExpr)\n169|\tif !ok || selector.Sel.Name != \"EOF\" {\n170|\t\treturn false\n171|\t}\n172|\tident, ok := selector.X.(*ast.Ident)\n173|\treturn ok && ident.Name == \"io\"\n174|}\n175|\n176|// hasRuneLiteral reports whether the subtree holds a rune\n177|// literal: wire delimiters and escapes, not domain facts.\n178|func hasRuneLiteral(node ast.Node) bool {\n179|\tfound := false\n180|\tast.Inspect(node, func(inner ast.Node) bool {\n181|\t\tliteral, ok := inner.(*ast.BasicLit)\n182|\t\tif ok && literal.Kind == token.CHAR {\n183|\t\t\tfound = true\n184|\t\t\treturn false\n185|\t\t}\n186|\t\treturn true\n187|\t})\n188|\treturn found\n189|}\n190|\n191|// identityRegistrations rosters every derived gate. domain\n192|// \"envelope-echo\" feeds the TestEnvelopeEchoEmptyStringRefuses\n193|// tripwire so that table cannot go stale.\n194|var identityRegistrations = []identityRegistration{\n195|\t// context.go.\n196|\t{id: `context.go|CheckFreshSink|authority.Mode != \"fresh_sink\"|0`, exempt: true, reason: \"dispatch, not a refusal: mode comes from validObjectMode, so \\\"\\\" is refused upstream\"},\n197|\t{id: `context.go|DecodeSourceSelector|count != 1|0`, driver: \"TestDecodeSourceSelectorComplement\", reason: \"exactly-one selector via none/all combos\"},\n198|\t{id: `context.go|VerifyRequestDigest|digest.String() != context.RequestDigest|0`, driver: \"TestIdentityZeroRows\", reason: \"zero request digest refuses at VerifyRequestDigest\"},\n199|\t// discovery.go: the sealed binding. Zero flips on both sides\n200|\t// are driven; non-zero flips were already pinned by\n(more lines below)"}}}
