{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5bd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07518-079c-74f3-9ecd-fd15c4068145"},"sequence":313,"recorded_at":1780531400000621,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5"},"call_id":"call_01a07518c00d7f308ff1126d79a06b9c","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2z3se0/TASK-260830-2z3se0_review-verdict-rev6.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2z3se0 — reviewer verdict, CR revision 6\n2|\n3|- Verdict: **changes requested** → `to-dev`\n4|- repeat-of: `rev5/F1` **and** `rev5/F2` — same class, third consecutive round:\n5|  the census's own unqualified sentence is false for a shape it does not derive.\n6|  See \"Routing note\" — the next step is a bounded stated-bound fix, not another\n7|  derivation widening.\n8|- Candidate tree `289f5f9bf3ee2dd5f4be1f69950c49fb8510420b`, base\n9|  `1cb6b93585749df4ef4755ce93e486bcde9e3a6b`, verified equal to the worktree\n10|  before the first probe and after the last one\n11|  (`git read-tree HEAD && git add -A && git write-tree`).\n12|- Run: `RUN-260906-245a60`. **445 mutants applied** by byte offset, PRESENT-asserted,\n13|  restored by byte-copy with a full-content comparison; **428 measured** (the 17\n14|  that could not compile were re-typed by hand and re-measured, not counted as\n15|  passes). **0 restore failures, 0 NOT-APPLIED, 0 unmeasured rows.**\n16|\n17|## Gate results\n18|\n19|| Gate | Result |\n20|| --- | --- |\n21|| G-A — settle `conditional` at `CheckTargetWriteGates` | **passes** |\n22|| G-B — shapes covered over shapes that exist, denominator built independently | **fails** (F1) |\n23|| G-C — re-run the battery; behavioural vs census-only; resurrections; survivors | **passes** |\n24|\n25|Baseline before any mutant: `go build ./...` 0, `go vet ./...` 0,\n26|`gofmt -l internal/` clean, `go test ./... -count=1` 17/17 ok (29.3s),\n27|`tracecheck` 0 (`acceptance_cases=88`).\n28|\n29|## G-A — settled, and settled in the direction the rev5 question left open\n30|\n31|Round 5 asked whether the decode-side coherence gate makes `conditional`\n32|unreachable at `CheckTargetWriteGates`, or whether a write gate admits a status\n33|it must refuse. The producer answered the first half correctly — it does **not**\n34|make it unreachable, because `CheckTargetWriteGates` and `CapabilityUsable` are\n35|exported and take caller-built maps — and pinned the clause at every site. I did\n36|not take that on report. Six targeted probes, each keeping the gate present and\n37|admitting exactly one member of the rejected class:\n38|\n39|| probe | narrows to | verdict | named failing test |\n40|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n41|| GA1 `CapabilityUsable` status clause admits `capabilityStatuses[1]` | conditional+enabled usable | BEHAVIOURAL-KILL | `TestCapabilityNonAvailableEnabledIsNotUsable/conditional/enabled` |\n42|| GA2 `capabilityMapUsable` same | conditional+enabled reaches the write gate | BEHAVIOURAL-KILL | `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled` (4 subtests) + the unit test |\n43|| GA3 provider side admits conditional | conditional provider usable | BEHAVIOURAL-KILL | `…/conditional_provider` |\n44|| GA4 decode coherence gate exempts `conditional` | decoded probe carries conditional+enabled | BEHAVIOURAL-KILL | `TestCapabilityStatusMatrix`, `TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry` |\n45|| GA5 `CheckContextEcho` admits any same-length mismatch | rebuilt context of equal length | BEHAVIOURAL-KILL | `TestCheckContextEcho` |\n46|| GA6 doctor required-capability check exempts conditional | doctor healthy with a conditional capability | BEHAVIOURAL-KILL | `TestCheckDoctorHealthyDrivesEveryRequiredCapability`, `TestDoctorResultRules` |\n47|\n48|GA2 is the exact probe the rev5 verdict asked for and it fails at\n49|`CheckTargetWriteGates`, not only at the unit predicate. GA4 shows the two\n50|halves of the belt-and-braces pair are independently pinned: neither is carrying\n51|the other. **G-A is closed. Do not re-open it.**\n52|\n53|## G-C — 445 mutants applied / 428 measured, behavioural kills separated from census-only\n54|\n55|Killers are classified the rev5 way: a failure whose only failing top-level\n56|tests are the source-text censuses is `CENSUS-ONLY`, never a behavioural kill.\n57|Census set: `TestIdentityGatesAreCensused`, `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused`,\n58|`TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction`, `TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`,\n59|`TestNoUnregisteredInlineVocabularies`, `TestAxerrorImportsAreUnaliased`,\n60|`TestAllProductionSwitchesAreClassified`, `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec`,\n61|`TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`, `TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed`,\n62|`TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived`.\n63|\n64|| Battery | applied | behavioural kills | survived | census-only |\n65|| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n66|| A — helper bound edges, **WIDEN** (admits a member it must reject) | 101 | 93 | 8 | 0 |\n67|| A — helper bound edges, **NARROW** (rejects a member it must admit) | 118 | 97 | 21 | 0 |\n68|| C — `len` guards | 9 | 8 | 1 | 0 |\n69|| D — identity gates, both operands, both spellings | 156 | 94 | 0 | 62 |\n70|| E — hand-typed re-runs of D's 17 non-compiling rows | 17 | 10 | 0 | 7 |\n71|| E2 — shape controls for 4 of E (no `len` introduced) | 4 | 0 | 0 | 4 |\n72|| G-A — targeted capability/echo probes | 6 | 6 | 0 | 0 |\n73|| G-B — census blind-spot plants and controls | 8 | 1 | 3 | 4 |\n74|| R — the rev5 survivors my generator does not emit | 9 | 0 | 9 | 0 |\n75|| **total measured** | **428** | **309** | **42** | **77** |\n76|\n77|(The log carries 445 rows: the 428 above plus the 17 `COMPILE-FAIL` attempts that\n78|battery E replaces.)\n79|\n80|The battery is generated from production syntax, not from the census\n81|registries: every INT literal argument of every one of the six bound helpers is\n82|moved by one in **both** directions, every `len` comparison literal is moved\n83|outward, and **both operands** of every derived identity gate are widened to\n84|exempt their zero. D's 17 rows that could not compile (`go vet`'s\n85|`redundant or`, or a non-string operand) were **re-typed by hand and re-measured**\n86|rather than counted as passes — an unmeasured row is not a kill.\n87|\n88|### Identity class: 173 measured rows, **0 survivors**\n89|\n90|Every one of the 173 rows (156 generated + 17 hand-typed) either produces a\n91|behavioural kill or is `CENSUS-ONLY` on a row that says exactly why. I checked\n92|all 7 hand-typed `CENSUS-ONLY` results against their registry rows rather than\n93|accepting the classification:\n94|\n95|- 4 × `previous != \"\"` sentinels (`checkExcludedClasses`, `checkRequiredDispositions`,\n96|  `checkContractsShape` ×2) — rows say \"first-iteration sortedness sentinel, not a\n97|  fact gate\". A control re-shape (`&& previous != \"a\"`, introducing no `len` row)\n98|  is likewise census-only. Consistent with the declared role.\n99|- `decode.go|rawUint53|literal == \"\"` — row says defensive/unreachable. Correct:\n100|  `json.Number.String` never yields an empty literal.\n101|- `CheckCallBinding|context.Environment != admitted` — the *admitted* side dies\n102|  (`TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse`); the caller side is census-only, exactly\n103|  as the row's \"caller side unreachable, tuple always decoded\" says.\n104|- `CheckTupleAdmission|entry.Key.Environment != environment` — the *entry* side\n105|  dies (`TestTupleAdmissionZeroFactsRefuse`); the probed side is the row's stated\n106|  hand-built-`Tuple{}` bound.\n107|\n108|**No unmeasured fact side. No unstated identity survivor.**\n109|\n110|### Bound class, admit direction: 18 widening survivors, **all rostered**\n111|\n112|| survivor | registry disposition | verified |\n113|| --- | --- | --- |\n114|| `manifest.go\\|DecodeManifest\\|checkSortedUniqueStrings\\|\"platforms\"` element-min 1→0, element-max 16→17, count-max 4→5 | exempt: \"equivalent … unreachable behind `scalar.ParsePlatform` and the four-name closed set\" | yes — every element runs through `scalar.ParsePlatform`; a fifth member does not exist. rev5 noted the element *minimum* is not spelled out in the row wording; it still is not. |\n115|| 5 × `65536` count ceilings (`canonical_event_ids`, `canonical_event_candidate_ids`, `raw_reference_ids`, `required_source_object_ids`, `created_resource_keys`) | exempt: \"stated bound: 65537 digests\" | yes |\n116|| `decode.go\\|checkExtensions\\|len(name) < 3` → `< 2` | exempt: \"no 2-character key satisfies the reverse-DNS grammar\" | yes |\n117|| 8 × `maxUint53` maxima → `maxUint53+1` | census header class-level stated bound; `parseUint53Literal` refuses above `maxUint53` at parse time | yes — `TestUint53RepresentabilityCeiling` proves the mechanism |\n118|| `protocol.go\\|bytesTrimSpace\\|len(trimmed) == 0` → `== 1` | rostered plumbing, a trim helper with no refusal | yes |\n119|\n120|**No unstated widening survivor.** This reproduces rev5's finding on byte-identical\n121|production.\n122|\n123|### Bound class, accept direction — new measurement, reported not charged\n124|\n125|I also ran the direction rev5 did not: 118 mutants that *tighten* a bound\n126|(min→min+1, max→max−1). **21 survive**, meaning no test supplies a value at the\n127|accepted edge itself — e.g. `context.go|DecodeReadAuthority|\"root_handle_names\"`\n128|admits elements of length 1..128 and no test drives a 1-character or a 128-character\n129|element. All 21 sit on rows that name a driver.\n130|\n131|This is **not** a rework item: the DoD's mutant requirement is the admit\n132|direction, and that direction passes 93 of 101 with every survivor rostered.\n133|I record it because the bound census header claims its drivers drive\n134|\"min-1/min/max/max+1\", and for these 21 sites they drive the refusal side only.\n135|Fold it into the stated bound if you touch the header for F1; do not open a\n136|round on it.\n137|\n138|### Resurrections: none, and none possible\n139|\n140|- `git diff c0174e87 289f5f9b -- '*.go' ':(exclude)*_test.go'` is **empty**.\n141|  Production is byte-identical to rev5, and rev5 established it byte-identical\n142|  to rev4. The three changed files are `bound_census_test.go`,\n143|  `identity_census_test.go`, `probe_test.go`.\n144|- Test inventory diffed across the two trees: **103 → 109 top-level tests, 6\n145|  added, 0 removed.** `probe_test.go` is pure addition (+75/−0). A kill cannot\n146|  resurrect against identical production and a strict superset of tests.\n147|- rev5's 13 survivors: all 13 re-measured, **none moved**. My generator emits 10\n148|  of them directly; the remaining 3 classes (`maxUint53` maxima, the\n149|  `bytesTrimSpace` trim guard) were run as battery R and survive with the same\n150|  verified rationale.\n151|\n152|## AC coverage — 7 of 7\n153|\n154|| AC row | production call site | named driving tests |\n155|| --- | --- | --- |\n156|| discovery | `internal/sessadapter/discovery.go` `Discover` | `TestDiscoverBindsManifestToCandidate`, `TestDiscoverRefusals` |\n157|| manifest | `manifest.go` `DecodeManifest` | `TestDecodeManifestAcceptsFixture`, `TestDecodeManifestValueRules` |\n158|| probe | `probe.go` `DecodeProbe` | `TestDecodeProbeAcceptsFixture`, `TestDecodeProbeClosedRules` |\n159|| closed operations | `operations.go` `CheckRequestBody` | `TestEveryOperationHasContractVectors`, derived-vector suite |\n160|| limits | `context.go` `DecodeResourceLimits` | `TestDecodeResourceLimitsBounds` |\n161|| idempotency | `context.go` `VerifyRequestDigest` | `TestRequestDigestFixpoint` + echo suite |\n162|| tuple gates | `tuple.go` `CheckTupleAdmission` | `TestCheckTupleAdmissionRefusals` |\n163|\n164|`tracecheck` exit 0 validates every declaration and test path in the registry.\n165|The AC's crash/idempotency clause is declared vacuous with a stated bound\n166|(`doc.go`: the package mutates no durable state; the idempotency it enforces is\n167|the request-digest binding, the byte-for-byte context echo, and the fresh-sink\n168|rule) and the README says the Section 7.8 clause binding stays `unevidenced`\n169|rather than claiming clause coverage. Honest — no unsupported claim.\n170|\n171|---\n172|\n173|## F1 — G-B was asked and not answered; three shapes are open, one with a live production instance\n174|\n175|`repeat-of: rev5/F1` (a spelling the identity census cannot derive) and\n176|`rev5/F2` (a declaration context neither census descends into).\n177|\n178|The brief asked, for each extended census, \"what is the shape after this one?\"\n179|and closed with \"If any is genuinely out of scope, that is a bound to write\n180|down, not a silence.\" The rework evidence discusses none of the three shapes it\n181|named, reports no shapes ratio, and neither census header gained a stated bound.\n182|Both headers still carry their unqualified sentence:\n183|\n184|- `identity_census_test.go:21` — *\"A new identity gate with no row fails the census.\"*\n185|- `bound_census_test.go:25` — *\"A new bound with no row fails the census.\"*\n186|\n187|I built the denominator independently of the registries (a `go/ast` shape scan\n188|of the eight production files) and probed each shape with a plant. **8 probes;\n189|each plant added to production, then `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, and\n190|`go test ./... -count=1` across all 17 packages:**\n191|\n192|| shape | probe | result |\n193|| --- | --- | --- |\n194|| identity gate spelled `bytes.Equal` | `if !bytes.Equal(received, sent) { return errors.New(…) }` | **SURVIVED** — build 0, vet 0, whole repo green, unrostered |\n195|| identity gate + `len` bound inside a **package-level func literal** | `var zzProbeLiteralGate = func(observed, expected string) error { if observed != expected {…}; if len(observed) > 4096 {…} }` | **SURVIVED** — invisible to *both* censuses |\n196|| bound whose comparison holds no `len` call | `length := len(value); if length < 1 \\|\\| length > 4096 {…}` | **SURVIVED** |\n197|| bound helper through a struct field | `zzProbeChecker{bound: requireStringBounds}` then `checker.bound(…)` | covered — `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused` reports the indirection |\n198|| constructor through a function that returns it | `func f() func(axerror.Spec)… { return axerror.New }` | covered — `TestRefusalConstructorsMatchProduction` |\n199|| tagged-switch arm made unreachable | `case OpDoctor:` → `case Operation(\"doctor-zz\"):` | covered — `TestEveryArmWitnessRefusesAtTheProductionEntry` |\n200|| control: the same `!=` gate as a `FuncDecl` | — | reddens `TestIdentityGatesAreCensused`, naming the site |\n201|| control: the same code as a `FuncDecl` | — | reddens **both** censuses |\n202|\n203|The two controls make the probes fair: identical code in a `FuncDecl` is caught;\n204|the same code one declaration level up is not.\n205|\n206|**Shapes covered over shapes that exist, denominator built independently:**\n207|\n208|- identity-decision shapes: `==`/`!=` BinaryExpr ✓, tagged switch ✓ (switch\n209|  census allows only `switch operation`), tagless switch ✓ (only\n210|  `readUTF16Escape`), map-presence ✓ (`presenceRegistrations`), inline\n211|  vocabulary chain ✓ (chain census), stdlib equality predicate ✗,\n212|  package-level func-literal scope ✗ → **5 of 7**\n213|- bound shapes: six helpers direct ✓, helper through any indirection ✓\n214|  (var/`:=`/assignment/argument/return/struct field/method value), `len`\n215|  comparison in any statement context ✓, cross-field relational — stated ✓,\n216|  `maxUint53` maxima — stated ✓, length through a variable ✗, package-level\n217|  func-literal scope ✗ → **5 of 7**\n218|- constructor shapes: direct, alias, import alias, returned-by-function, inline\n219|  outside a registered body → **5 of 5**\n220|\n221|**15 of 19; 4 open; 3 of the 4 demonstrated open by a plant that survives the\n222|entire repository suite.** (`utf8.RuneCountInString`/`cap` as a direct bound\n223|source is the fourth; I did not plant it — its only live use is inside\n224|`stringLength`, whose callers are rostered, so it has no live gap today.)\n225|\n226|Two of the four are not hypothetical:\n227|\n228|1. **`context.go:222` `CheckContextEcho`** is a live identity gate —\n229|   `if !bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw) { failProtocol(\"success context does\n230|   not echo the request context byte-for-byte\", \"context\") }` — doing exactly the\n231|   echo-identity job this census was built for, in a spelling the census cannot\n232|   derive, with no row and no stated bound. It is behaviourally covered today:\n233|   GA5 narrows it to admit any same-length mismatch and\n234|   `TestCheckContextEcho` fails. So this is a durability finding, not a live\n235|   hole — the same standing rev5/F1's two `discovery.go` rows had.\n236|2. **`protocol.go:126-155`** already ships seven package-level func literals (the\n237|   refusal constructors). The constructor census descends into them by design\n238|   (\"the set of package-level func-valued vars whose body constructs an error\").\n239|   The identity and bound censuses do not. The fix that was ported to one\n240|   instrument was not ported to the other two — the rev5/F2 shape again.\n241|\n242|### What closes this\n243|\n244|Either extend the two derivations, or — better — **write the bound down**. Add to\n245|each census header a \"Stated bounds\" clause naming what the derivation does not\n246|see, and qualify the two unqualified sentences to the shapes actually derived.\n247|Concretely: `bytes.Equal`/stdlib equality predicates, declaration contexts other\n248|than `FuncDecl` bodies, and length values bound to a variable before comparison.\n249|If you extend a derivation instead, the accompanying stated bound is still\n250|required, because the next shape after the extension will exist too.\n251|\n252|### Routing note for the orchestrator\n253|\n254|This is the third consecutive round on one class: rev4/N8, rev5/F1+F2, now this.\n255|Each round's extension closed the shape that was found and left the next one, and\n256|I can demonstrate that directly — the shapes I plant today are the shapes the\n257|rev5 fixes did not reach. Per the repeat-of rule this should be a **gate**, not an\n258|open-ended seventh derivation-widening round. The bounded ask above (a stated\n259|bound plus two qualified sentences, no new derivation required) is what I would\n260|route; an equally defensible call is to accept the CR on a policy decision that\n261|an unqualified census sentence is acceptable given the behavioural evidence, and\n262|record the four open shapes on the Story so the two following leaves inherit them\n263|explicitly. That call is the orchestrator's, not mine — but it should not be made\n264|by silence, which is what the current revision does.\n265|\n266|## Explicitly closed — do not re-litigate in round 7\n267|\n268|- G-A, the capability-status class, at all three sites plus the decode coherence\n269|  gate and the doctor required-capability path. Six probes, six behavioural kills.\n270|- The identity class over its production-derived denominator: 173 rows, 0\n271|  survivors, every exemption verified against the code.\n272|- The bound class in the admit direction: 101+9 widening mutants, 18 survivors,\n273|  every one on a committed row or the census's declared class-level stated bound.\n274|- Resurrections: impossible by construction; production byte-identical to rev4\n275|  and rev5, zero tests removed.\n276|- AC coverage 7 of 7; README/tracecheck claims honest (`acceptance_cases=88`,\n277|  Section 7.8 clause binding disclosed as `unevidenced`).\n278|- The bound accept-direction survivors (21) — measured and reported above, not a\n279|  rework item.\n280|\n281|## Reproduction\n282|\n283|```bash\n284|# tree identity, before and after\n285|git read-tree HEAD && git add -A && git write-tree     # 289f5f9b…\n286|\n287|# rev5 -> rev6 production delta (empty)\n288|git diff c0174e8761518432e55ed5bdcf915959da9bd9f4 289f5f9bf3ee2dd5f4be1f69950c49fb8510420b \\\n289|  -- '*.go' ':(exclude)*_test.go'\n290|\n291|# G-B plants: add to internal/sessadapter/, then\n292|go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test ./... -count=1     # all three stay green\n293|#   zz_gb1.go  func zzProbeByteIdentity(received, sent []byte) error {\n294|#                  if !bytes.Equal(received, sent) { return errors.New(\"…\") }; return nil }\n295|#   zz_gb2.go  var zzProbeLiteralGate = func(observed, expected string) error {\n296|#                  if observed != expected { return errors.New(\"…\") }\n297|#                  if len(observed) > 4096 { return errors.New(\"…\") }; return nil }\n298|#   zz_gb3.go  func zzProbeLenVariable(value string) error {\n299|#                  length := len(value)\n300|#                  if length < 1 || length > 4096 { return errors.New(\"…\") }; return nil }\n301|# controls (must redden): the same bodies written as plain func declarations.\n302|\n303|# G-A\n304|#   probe.go CapabilityUsable / capabilityMapUsable:\n305|#     value.Status == \"available\"\n306|#       -> (value.Status == \"available\" || value.Status == capabilityStatuses[1])\n307|go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1     # red at\n308|#     TestCapabilityNonAvailableEnabledIsNotUsable and\n309|#     TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled\n310|```\n311|\n312|Battery log attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_review-battery-rev6-RUN-260906-245a60.log`\n313|(445 rows: mutant id, verdict, failing behavioural tests, failing census tests,\n314|restore check, wall time).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
