{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07518-079c-74f3-9ecd-fd15c4068145"},"sequence":339,"recorded_at":1780531400000673,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5"},"call_id":"call_01a07518c8867cb2bf8d727b17885584","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2z3se0/TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev6.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2z3se0 — round-6 rework evidence (review rev5 F1/F2/F3)\n2|\n3|Round 5 returned changes requested. All three findings were in the new\n4|instruments, not in shipped behaviour. This round reworks the instruments\n5|only: **zero production bytes changed** (all edits are in three\n6|`*_test.go` files under `internal/sessadapter/`).\n7|\n8|Files changed (working tree, uncommitted, per the no-commit shape):\n9|\n10|- `internal/sessadapter/identity_census_test.go` — F1\n11|- `internal/sessadapter/bound_census_test.go` — F2\n12|- `internal/sessadapter/probe_test.go` — F3\n13|\n14|## F1 — identity census now derives both spellings (was NEQ-only)\n15|\n16|`identityGatesInSyntax` derives every `!=` **and** `==` domain\n17|comparison with identical exclusions (nil/err/EOF/rune/len). 37\n18|`==` sites rostered: 31 driven, 6 exempt with upstream-guard\n19|rationales verified against the code (validObjectMode,\n20|validValidateMode, validTupleEntryStatus, checkStringBounds\n21|1..4096, TestResumePlanIdentityComplement; the two caller-param\n22|dispatches state their deterministic branch).\n23|\n24|- `discovery.go:105,112` (`== \"\"` zero refusals) are now rows\n25|  (`discover` domain, driver `TestDiscoverRefusals`).\n26|- 20 vocabulary-table membership positives are rows driven by the\n27|  new `TestVocabularyMembershipRefusesEmpty`, which refuses `\"\"`\n28|  and `\"bogus\"` at every loop plus `validRole`, `validCandidateKind`,\n29|  and `operationSkipsRequestContext` (tables stay pinned by\n30|  `TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`).\n31|- `decode.go|rawUint53|literal == \"\"` is the single defensive\n32|  exemption: unreachable because `json.Number.String` never yields\n33|  an empty literal and every non-number is refused at the decode\n34|  arms above.\n35|- 4 EQL canaries added; census now rosters 99 gates (85 driven,\n36|  14 exempt). The unqualified sentence (\"a new identity gate with\n37|  no row fails the census\") is true again for both spellings.\n38|- Synthetic `TestIdentityScanSeesBothSpellings` proves the split,\n39|  including the exact rev5 probe shape (`observed == expected`).\n40|\n41|## F2 — bound census: indirection gate + any-context len derivation\n42|\n43|Ported the constructor-census shape (review rev4/N8 fix) to the six\n44|bound helpers rather than adding a `var`-form case:\n45|\n46|- `boundHelperIndirections` flags **any** use of a helper name that\n47|  is neither a direct call (`Fun` of the enclosing call) nor one of\n48|  the six definitions — var/:=/assignment/argument/return, package\n49|  or function scope, uniformly. A helper alias fails as a census\n50|  violation instead of hiding every bound built through it.\n51|- The `len` pass walks every `BinaryExpr` in the function body, not\n52|  just `if` conditions — covering `for`/`switch`/`return`/\n53|  assignment contexts. Production today gains exactly the six\n54|  reviewer-predicted loop indices (`decode.go` x4, `tuple.go` x2),\n55|  all rostered as plumbing-exempt with the suite that pins each\n56|  loop (`TestSortedUniqueBoundEdges`, surrogate agreement suite,\n57|  `TestUint53RepresentabilityCeiling`).\n58|- Census now rosters 103 sites (80 driven, 23 exempt); 2 for-context\n59|  canaries added.\n60|- Synthetic `TestBoundHelperIndirectionReports` (package-level and\n61|  function-local alias report; direct call and definition exempt)\n62|  and `TestBoundLenScanSeesNonIfContexts` (return/for/switch/assign\n63|  derive; boundless `make` length does not) prove both halves.\n64|\n65|## F3 — conditional+enabled settled: refused, and now pinned\n66|\n67|Resolution: **no live hole** — the behaviour was already correct;\n68|what was missing was the pin and the stated reasoning.\n69|\n70|- `decodeCapabilityValue` refuses `enabled=true` with non-`available`\n71|  status at the boundary (pinned by `TestCapabilityStatusMatrix`),\n72|  which keeps decoded probes clean. But `CapabilityUsable` and\n73|  `capabilityMapUsable` also take caller-built values, so their\n74|  `== \"available\"` clauses independently refuse\n75|  `conditional`+`enabled` — today, at both sites.\n76|- New `TestCapabilityNonAvailableEnabledIsNotUsable` drives\n77|  hand-built conditional/unsupported/unknown x enabled true/false\n78|  through both predicates (usable only for available+enabled).\n79|- New `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled` drives\n80|  hand-built conditional+enabled through `CheckTargetWriteGates`\n81|  on every required adapter capability and the provider side.\n82|- The admit-conditional widening now fails at both sites (M-F3a/b\n83|  below) — the probe the verdict asked for, failing if the decode\n84|  gate were the only thing standing between `conditional` and a\n85|  target write.\n86|\n87|## Mutant battery (this round, byte-offset edits, sha256-restored)\n88|\n89|Scored the reviewer's way: a failure whose only failing tests are\n90|source-text censuses is `census-only`, never a behavioural kill.\n91|Instrument plants (dead/uncalled code) can only ever be\n92|census-only — that is the correct signal for them, not a gap.\n93|\n94|| mutant | narrows the gate to | named failing test(s) | class |\n95||---|---|---|---|\n96|| M-F1a: `ExecutablePath == \"\"` -> `== \"\\x00\"` | admits the empty path | `TestDiscoverRefusals` | behavioural |\n97|| M-F1b: `purpose == allowed` -> `... \\|\\| purpose == \"\"` | admits `\"\"` purpose | `TestVocabularyMembershipRefusesEmpty` | behavioural |\n98|| M-F1d: `Severity == \"error\"` -> `== \"err\"` | admits error findings as valid | `TestValidateResultRules` (+ witness) | behavioural |\n99|| M-F1e: `strategy == \"archive_only\"` -> `== \"archive-only\"` | admits archive_only target | `TestCheckTupleAdmissionRefusals` (+ witness) | behavioural |\n100|| M-F1c-probe: reviewer `==` plant, uncalled | new unrostered gate | `TestIdentityGatesAreCensused` only | census-only (correct: dead code) |\n101|| M-F1c-control: reviewer `!=` control, uncalled | new unrostered gate | `TestIdentityGatesAreCensused` only | census-only |\n102|| M-F2a: reviewer `var zzprobeIndirect` plant | hidden bound site | `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused` (indirection) only | census-only (correct: dead code) |\n103|| M-F2b: reviewer return-`len` plant | hidden bound site | `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused` only | census-only (correct: dead code) |\n104|| M-F2c: reviewer `for`-`len` plant | hidden bound site | `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused` only | census-only (correct: dead code) |\n105|| M-F2d: control direct helper call | new unrostered site | `TestBoundGuardsAreCensused` only | census-only |\n106|| M-F2e: cursor max `1024` -> `1025` | admits 1025-char cursor | `TestRequestScalarBoundEdges` | behavioural |\n107|| M-F3a: `CapabilityUsable` admits `capabilityStatuses[1]` | conditional+enabled usable | `TestCapabilityNonAvailableEnabledIsNotUsable` | behavioural |\n108|| M-F3b: `capabilityMapUsable` admits `capabilityStatuses[1]` | conditional+enabled write gate admits | `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`, `TestCapabilityNonAvailableEnabledIsNotUsable` | behavioural |\n109|| M-F3c: provider side admits conditional | conditional provider usable | `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled/conditional_provider` | behavioural |\n110|\n111|Zero survivors. Every mutant restored byte-identical (snapshot\n112|check passed, no extra files left). One harness note: the first\n113|run of this battery restored via `git checkout`, which is a no-op\n114|on the untracked `sessadapter/` tree, so four edits cascaded and\n115|those verdicts were discarded; the battery was re-run with\n116|byte-copy backup/restore and the table above is from the clean\n117|run only.\n118|\n119|## Gates (all exit 0, run this round)\n120|\n121|- `go build ./...` — exit 0\n122|- `go vet ./...` — exit 0\n123|- `GOOS=windows go vet ./internal/sessadapter/` — exit 0\n124|- `gofmt -l internal/` — clean\n125|- `go test ./... -count=1` — 17/17 packages ok, zero FAIL\n126|- `go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -count=1 -race` — exit 0\n127|- `tracecheck` — exit 0, acceptance_cases=88\n128|\n129|## Coverage ratios (new/changed rows this round)\n130|\n131|- F1: 37 of 37 derived `==` rows rostered (31 driven, 6 exempt\n132|  with code-checked rationales); every driven row names its\n133|  production call site and driver above.\n134|- F2: 6 of 6 newly derived `len` rows rostered (plumbing-exempt);\n135|  indirection shape proven by synthetic gate tests.\n136|- F3: 2 of 2 usability `==` rows driven by hand-built\n137|  conditional+enabled vectors through `CapabilityUsable` and\n138|  `CheckTargetWriteGates` (provider side pinned too).\n139|\n140|AC rows from prior rounds are unchanged (10 of 10 per the\n141|round-1..5 evidence chain); this round adds instrument closure,\n142|no production behaviour.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07518-079c-74f3-9ecd-fd15c4068145"},"sequence":340,"recorded_at":1780531400000675,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5"},"call_id":"call_01a07518c9b27e43937ace8d0679debb","text":"Read text file `internal/sessadapter/identity_census_test.go`.\n(399 line(s) above)\n400|\t}\n401|\tvar orphaned []string\n402|\tfor id, count := range registeredCounts {\n403|\t\tfor i := derivedCounts[id]; i < count; i++ {\n404|\t\t\torphaned = append(orphaned, id)\n405|\t\t}\n406|\t}\n407|\tsort.Strings(unregistered)\n408|\tsort.Strings(orphaned)\n409|\tif len(unregistered) > 0 {\n410|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"production identity gate(s) with no census row:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(unregistered, \"\\n  \"))\n411|\t}\n412|\tif len(orphaned) > 0 {\n413|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"census row(s) naming no production gate:\\n  %s\", strings.Join(orphaned, \"\\n  \"))\n414|\t}\n415|\tdriven, exempt := 0, 0\n416|\tfor _, row := range identityRegistrations {\n417|\t\tif row.exempt {\n418|\t\t\texempt++\n419|\t\t} else {\n420|\t\t\tdriven++\n421|\t\t}\n422|\t}\n423|\tt.Logf(\"identity census: %d gates rostered (%d driven, %d exempt) across production\", len(derived), driven, exempt)\n424|}\n425|\n426|// TestIdentityScanSeesBothSpellings proves the spelling split of\n427|// the derivation against synthetic files: an ==-spelled refusal\n428|// and a !=-spelled refusal are both derived, while the\n429|// mechanical classes stay excluded in both spellings. The\n430|// vectors are synthetic on purpose: they prove the gate, not\n431|// production. This is the regression test for review rev5/F1,\n432|// where the NEQ-only scan passed an ==-spelled plant silently.\n433|func TestIdentityScanSeesBothSpellings(t *testing.T) {\n434|\tparse := func(source string) *ast.File {\n435|\t\tt.Helper()\n436|\t\tsyntax, err := parser.ParseFile(token.NewFileSet(), \"probe.go\", []byte(source), 0)\n437|\t\tif err != nil {\n438|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parse synthetic source: %v\", err)\n439|\t\t}\n440|\t\treturn syntax\n441|\t}\n442|\tderived := func(source string) []string {\n443|\t\tt.Helper()\n444|\t\treturn identityGatesInSyntax(parse(source), \"probe.go\")\n445|\t}\n446|\tcontains := func(ids []string, want string) bool {\n447|\t\tt.Helper()\n448|\t\tfor _, id := range ids {\n449|\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(id, want) {\n450|\t\t\t\treturn true\n451|\t\t\t}\n452|\t\t}\n453|\t\treturn false\n454|\t}\n455|\tt.Run(\"equality refusal derives\", func(t *testing.T) {\n456|\t\tids := derived(\"package probe\\nfunc zzProbeEqualityRefusal(observed, expected string) error {\\nif observed == expected { return nil }\\nreturn json.Unmarshal(nil, nil)\\n}\\n\")\n457|\t\tif !contains(ids, \"probe.go|zzProbeEqualityRefusal|observed == expected|\") {\n458|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived = %v, want the equality refusal\", ids)\n459|\t\t}\n460|\t})\n461|\tt.Run(\"inequality refusal derives\", func(t *testing.T) {\n462|\t\tids := derived(\"package probe\\nfunc zzProbeInequalityRefusal(observed, expected string) bool {\\nif observed != expected { return false }\\nreturn true\\n}\\n\")\n463|\t\tif !contains(ids, \"probe.go|zzProbeInequalityRefusal|observed != expected|\") {\n464|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived = %v, want the inequality refusal\", ids)\n465|\t\t}\n466|\t})\n467|\tt.Run(\"mechanical classes stay excluded in both spellings\", func(t *testing.T) {\n468|\t\tids := derived(\"package probe\\nfunc zzMechanical(a, b string, err error) bool {\\nif err == nil { return false }\\nif a == b && len(a) == 1 { return true }\\nreturn a != b\\n}\\n\")\n469|\t\tfor _, id := range ids {\n470|\t\t\tif strings.Contains(id, \"err ==\") || strings.Contains(id, \"len(a)\") {\n471|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived = %v, want the nil and length plumbing excluded\", ids)\n472|\t\t\t}\n473|\t\t}\n474|\t\tif !contains(ids, \"probe.go|zzMechanical|a != b|\") {\n475|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived = %v, want the domain inequality kept\", ids)\n476|\t\t}\n477|\t})\n478|}\n479|\n480|// TestVocabularyMembershipRefusesEmpty drives every\n481|// vocabulary-table membership loop with the empty string: \"\" is\n482|// outside every closed union, so every loop must report false,\n483|// and a mutant admitting \"\" at any one loop (`x == allowed || x\n484|// == \"\"`) fails here. A bogus non-empty member is refused too,\n485|// pinning the loop against an arbitrary widening. The tables\n486|// themselves stay pinned by\n487|// TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered; this test pins the\n488|// consultation. It is the named driver of every domain\n489|// \"vocabulary\" row.\n490|func TestVocabularyMembershipRefusesEmpty(t *testing.T) {\n491|\tstrings := map[string]func(string) bool{\n492|\t\t\"validFindingSeverity\":     validFindingSeverity,\n493|\t\t\"validObjectMode\":          validObjectMode,\n494|\t\t\"validObjectPurpose\":       validObjectPurpose,\n495|\t\t\"validReadPurpose\":         validReadPurpose,\n496|\t\t\"validFidelityProfile\":     validFidelityProfile,\n497|\t\t\"validValidateMode\":        validValidateMode,\n498|\t\t\"validCapabilityEvidence\":  validCapabilityEvidence,\n499|\t\t\"validCapabilityStatus\":    validCapabilityStatus,\n500|\t\t\"validRegistryEntryStatus\": validRegistryEntryStatus,\n501|\t\t\"validCapabilityName\":      validCapabilityName,\n502|\t\t\"validOperation\":           validOperation,\n503|\t\t\"validDirection\":           validDirection,\n504|\t\t\"validTupleEntryStatus\":    validTupleEntryStatus,\n505|\t\t\"validEvidenceResult\":      validEvidenceResult,\n506|\t\t\"validStrategy\":            validStrategy,\n507|\t\t\"validDisposition\":         validDisposition,\n508|\t\t\"validCaptureClass\":        validCaptureClass,\n509|\t\t\"validTupleArchitecture\":   validTupleArchitecture,\n510|\t}\n511|\tif len(strings) != 18 {\n512|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"string loops = %d, want one per string membership gate\", len(strings))\n513|\t}\n514|\tfor name, loop := range strings {\n515|\t\tif loop(\"\") {\n516|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s(\\\"\\\") = true; the empty string is outside every union\", name)\n517|\t\t}\n518|\t\tif loop(\"bogus\") {\n519|\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s(\\\"bogus\\\") = true; an arbitrary member is outside every union\", name)\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
