{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d0c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07518-079c-74f3-9ecd-fd15c4068145"},"sequence":1725,"recorded_at":1780531400003445,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"368dc5f6-65c1-4883-954e-0941c86fd7c5"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"7c39f995-5678-4bb5-8e4c-6d8e5ecd4430"},"task_id":"7c39f995-5678-4bb5-8e4c-6d8e5ecd4430","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"7c39f995-5678-4bb5-8e4c-6d8e5ecd4430","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-53-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat >> LOGBOOK.md <<'EOF'\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 7: rev6 G-B closed — shape space enumerated per census, three shapes derived, residue bounded\\n- FIX (identity): `identityGatesInSyntax` now derives `bytes.Equal` calls and visits package-level var initializers under their variable name (same scope rule as the constructor census; per-scope ordinals keep all existing rows identical). One live row added: `context.go|CheckContextEcho|bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw)` (domain `context-echo`, driver `TestCheckContextEcho`) — the live instance rev6 named. Header enumerates 8 identity-decision shapes (7 derived, 1 bound: other stdlib predicates) and qualifies the census sentence to derived shapes.\\n- FIX (bound): `boundSitesInSyntax` visits package-level var initializers and derives guards over length variables bound directly from `len(...)`/`stringLength(...)` (parens/conversions unwrap; `values := make(..., len(x))` binds no variable — proven by synthetic negative), plus direct `stringLength(...)` comparisons. Four live mechanism half-rows added (checkStringBounds + checkSortedUniqueStrings enforcements, exempt with caller-row drivers). Header enumerates 10 bound shapes (6 derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 bounded: decoded-value comparisons with live checkUint53Bounds:269, direct cap/RuneCount with none live) and folds in the 21 refusal-side-only drivers instead of claiming min/max admission per site.\\n- FIX (constructor): no derivation change (7/7 already); header enumerates the 7 construction shapes with residue (frameFault-via-alias, non-Go construction, out-of-dir/_test.go), plus synthetic proofs for failX in return/argument/struct-field positions and returned `axerror.New`.\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): the first length-var rule (RHS subtree contains len) over-derived on `values := make([]T, 0, len(elements))`, claiming element sortedness checks as len sites — tightened to direct binding; the P7 switch-arm plant kills at the arm witness entry, not the switch census (statement-vs-arm division of labor, now stated in the header); capability-clause and mechanism-comparison narrowings always co-fire their census by exact-render design — reported as behavioural kills with expected co-fire, never as clean singles.\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\nEOF\\necho \\\"LOGBOOK_APPENDED\\\"; tail -n 3 LOGBOOK.md | head -n 3\",\n  \"description\": \"Append round-7 logbook entry\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"LOGBOOK_APPENDED\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 992,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 248,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
